To deploy this React frontend as a Static Site on Render, follow these steps:
#
step 1. Clear Your Account View Since you are currently stuck on a Settings page, let's get you back to the main screen:

Click on the Render Logo or the word Dashboard at the very top-left corner of your screen.

Now, look at the top-right corner of the webpage and click the bright New + button.

Select Static Site from the drop-down menu (React apps are deployed as Static Sites on Render).
#
step 2. Connect Your Repository

Paste your Git URL (https://github.com/Magela84/azure-cost-dashboard.git) into the repository search box and click Connect.
#
step 3. Apply the React Specific Settings 

On the configuration screen, fill out the settings exactly like this so Render knows how to open and build your subfolder:
Name: azure-cost-dashboard-ui (or any name you prefer)
Branch: main

Root Directory: frontend (This tells Render to look inside your React folder instead of the main project folder)

Build Command: npm install && npm run build

Publish Directory: dist (or build, depending on what your React bundler outputs)

┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               Render Configuration Form                │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Root Directory:    frontend                            │
│ Build Command:     npm install && npm run build        │
│ Publish Directory: dist                                │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Render will pull the code from your frontend folder, install the packages, build your static files, and launch your live site!

